# Leantime Project Overview

Leantime is an open source project management system designed for non-project managers. It combines strategy, planning, and execution in an easy-to-use interface.

## Technology Stack
- **Backend**: PHP 8.2+, Laravel framework with custom components
- **Database**: MySQL 8.0+ or MariaDB 10.6+
- **Frontend**: Modern JavaScript (ES6+), Webpack (Laravel Mix), Less CSS, HTMX
- **Architecture**: Domain-driven design with plugin system

## Key Directories
- `app/Core/` - Framework core components and Laravel extensions
- `app/Domain/` - Application domains organized by feature
- `app/Plugins/` - Extension plugins
- `public/` - Web root with assets and themes
- `config/` - Configuration files
- `tests/` - Test files (Unit and Acceptance)

## Domain Structure
Each domain in `app/Domain/` contains:
- `Controllers/` - HTTP endpoints
- `Hxcontrollers/` - HTMX-specific controllers  
- `Repositories/` - Data access layer
- `Services/` - Business logic
- `Models/` - Data structures
- `Templates/` - View templates (Blade/PHP)
- `Js/` - Domain-specific JavaScript

## Development Commands
- `make run-dev` - Start development server (port 8090)
- `make build-dev` - Build for development
- `make build` - Build for production
- `make unit-test` - Run unit tests
- `make acceptance-test` - Run acceptance tests
- `php bin/leantime [command]` - CLI commands